---
export const title = 'Theming';
export const order = 500;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The art reads the theme's color tokens, so it follows your theme and dark mode with no extra work.
  To recolor every illustration at once, for example in brand colors, set the
  <code>--illustration-*-color</code> custom properties on <code>:root</code> or on a container:
  <code>--illustration-primary-color</code>, <code>--illustration-primary-container-color</code>,
  <code>--illustration-accent-color</code>, <code>--illustration-accent-alt-color</code>,
  <code>--illustration-surface-color</code>, <code>--illustration-inset-color</code>,
  <code>--illustration-backdrop-color</code>, <code>--illustration-outline-color</code> and
  <code>--illustration-detail-color</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'} inline>
  <div
    style='display: flex; gap: var(--spacing-200); --illustration-primary-color: var(--color-tertiary); --illustration-primary-container-color: var(--color-tertiary-container); --illustration-accent-color: var(--color-primary-container);'
  >
    <wc-illustration name='welcome'></wc-illustration>
    <wc-illustration name='empty-cart'></wc-illustration>
    <wc-illustration name='no-team'></wc-illustration>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  In high-contrast mode the soft fills drop out and every shape is outlined in the system text
  color, so the illustration still reads as line art.
</p>
